3. gnu path in containers
-------------------------
Rootless podman, one container/Containerfile for all of them (container/README),
a fresh clone per run (container/clean-room.sh), builds run by hand in the
container's shell.

Builds on x86_64, aarch64 (podman) and macOS on Apple Silicon (Docker) give
the same six files, byte for byte, at commit 4c52760 (default configuration).
Booting the output and make test-all were run on x86_64 only.

    image         gcc   linux-user emulator                   language flags
    ------------  ----  -----------------------------------   --------------
    Ubuntu 24.04  13    qemu-user-static                      default
    Debian 13     14.x  qemu-user-static (-static binaries)   default
    Ubuntu 26.04  15.x  qemu-user (no -static package)        -std=gnu17

(gcc: the cross gcc and the host gcc, of the same version.)

What the images needed (each is in the repository):
- Debian's cross gcc is --enable-default-pie: the PIC thunk in decomp.o breaks
  reset.bin's size accounting ("3796 bytes but header declares only 3764").
  decomp.o is built with -fno-pic -fno-pie.
- GCC 15 defaults to C23: the OBP engine and the host tools (mdgen's `false` as
  an enumeration constant, didepend.c) are built with -std=gnu17.
- Ubuntu 26.04 has no qemu-user-static package: qemu-user provides qemu-sparc64
  and qemu-sparc32plus. configure and release.sh look for NAME-static first,
  then NAME.
- `make all` begins with `clean`; the toolchain record of
  build/toolchain-check.sh is written again after it.
- Cloning a detached HEAD made Debian's git print its "initial branch" hint;
  release.sh and clean-room.sh clone with -c init.defaultBranch=main.
- `dwarf2genassym: Can't find snet_info` in the log of make all is expected
  (build/hv_reset/README.dwarf).

Not covered: make bootstrap-check (needs the host's binfmt_misc handlers),
Debian forky, the sun path.


4. gnu path, gcc 13 to 16 and binutils
---------------------------------------
Cross gcc (hypervisor, PROM): 13, 14, 15, 16. Host gcc (mdgen, mdlint; make md):
13.3, 14.4, 15.3, 16.2. GCC 15 and later need -std=gnu17
(build/hv_reset/gnu/README); without it mdgen stops on mdgen/basics.h:67,
`false` as an enumeration constant.

Full builds from scratch, cross gcc and host gcc of the same version
(./configure --with-gcc-cross --with-gcc, make all, make test; 13 is the
distribution's, with no options):

    gcc    binutils (as, ld)   language    make all
    ----   -----------------   ----------  --------
    13.3   2.42 Ubuntu, 2.47   default     22 s
    14.4   2.42 Ubuntu, 2.47   default     21 s
    15.3   2.42 Ubuntu, 2.47   -std=gnu17  21 s
    16.2   2.42 Ubuntu, 2.47   -std=gnu17  22 s
With each pair, `make all` passes and `make test` reaches the ok prompt. The
time is for 2.42. 2.47 is binutils 2.47.20260726 built from
ftp.gnu.org/gnu/binutils and used with `./configure --with-binutils-cross=DIR`
(`legion`); configure checks that the gcc runs the as and ld the build calls.

`make test-all` passes with each of them (smoke, md, boot, hv, workdir,
guards, obp); with a guest disk the `login` gate too: every gnu set (gcc
13.3, 14.4, 15.3 and 16.2 built from the distribution and from source, and
the containers' 14.2 and 15.2) reaches the login prompt in about 34 s.


5. sun path, Studio versions
----------------------------
Every Studio was built and booted to the OpenBoot ok prompt (`make test`).
Each is a full install in its own /opt directory, passed with
`--with-sun-studio=DIR`, and nothing else needs to change. They differ in:
- 12.2 and later need cc -xbuiltin=%none (build/cc-nobuiltin.sh); 12.2 needs
  -xdepend=no as well (build/cc-nobuiltin-nodepend.sh).
- 12.5 and 12.6 cannot start on an emulated T1 guest that does not declare
  VIS (their cc uses it; ld.so.1 refuses it): `isainfo -v` must list vis.
  ./configure checks that cc compiles and says so if not; the real T1 has no
  VIS, so on emulated hardware the declaration has to be added:
  https://unix0.cc/2026/10/05/sparc-vis-capability-mask/ (set on the guest for
  all the runs here).
- 12.6 writes no stabs (offsets.h from DWARF).
All are probed and handled; what ./configure checks: README.configure.

What ./configure measured for each (the count is of lines, so only zero or not
zero matters):

    Studio  cc    .stabs lines  _memcpy/_memset calls  then
    ------  ----  ------------  ---------------------  --------------------
    11      5.8   215           0
    12.0    5.9   218           0
    12.1    5.10  206           0
    12.2    5.11  206           2 (decomp.c)           -xbuiltin=%none
                                                       -xdepend=no
    12.3    5.12  206           2 (decomp.c)           -xbuiltin=%none
    12.4    5.13  206           2 (decomp.c)           -xbuiltin=%none
    12.5    5.14  206           2 (decomp.c)           -xbuiltin=%none
    12.6    5.15  0             4 (decomp.c, hv)       -xbuiltin=%none,
                                                       offsets.h from DWARF
The builds of one commit give a different q.bin and a different openboot.bin
for each Studio (the compiler differs); reset.bin and the MD blobs are the
same in all of them.

gmake all on the guest (Solaris under emulated QEMU), seconds, one run each,
nothing else running:

    Studio  11   12.0  12.1  12.2  12.3  12.4  12.5  12.6
    ------  ---  ----  ----  ----  ----  ----  ----  ----
    time    322  338   448   401   883   456   820   1305
Another run on the same machine can differ by a third. All give the same
1up-md.bin and 1up-hv.bin (the pins of blobs.sha256, the same as the gnu
path), and each set reaches the login prompt in about 34 s.

Each Studio's own assembler, bin/fbe, is not used by the build. Measured with
`fbe -xarch=v9d` on one rdhpr instruction: Studio 11 to 12.3 reject it cleanly
("invalid register"); 12.4, 12.5 and 12.6 accept it. The sun path uses the
system's /usr/ccs/bin/as (Studio 12.5, patch 118683-15) for every Studio.


6. offsets.h from DWARF
-----------------------
The hypervisor's assembler sources need the byte offsets of C struct members;
offsets.h holds them. Sun's makefiles make it with Sun's `stabs` tool, which
reads stabs debug info. gcc and Studio 12.6 cannot write stabs, so there
offsets.h is made from DWARF by dwarf2genassym.pl (build/hv_reset/gnu/README,
build/hv_reset/README.dwarf). The result is compared with the file Sun made
for ontario/legion:

    gnu  gcc 13.3, 14.4, 15.3, 16.2   each byte-identical to Sun's
                                      (gnu/reference/offsets.ontario-legion.h)
    sun  Developer Studio 12.6        byte-identical to Sun's
                                      (build/hv_reset/README.dwarf)
Sun Studio 11 to 12.5 write stabs, so `stabs` makes offsets.h there.


7. The OBP root dictionary rebuilt by the chain
------------------------------------------------
The OBP root, os/sun/sparc/forth.dic (the one shipped binary), replaced by a
dictionary the chain built itself (gnu path, legion, same OUTDIR,
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH fixed):

    root                                   openboot.bin
    ------------------------------------   ---------------
    shipped forth.dic                      reference
    forth32-xref.dic, built by the chain   identical to it
    f32t32.dic, built by the chain         identical to it
Both were themselves made by the chain from the shipped root, so one
generation from the seed is still needed. The build runs in a scratch directory
of fixed path length (build/obp/gnu/build-obp.sh), because the OBP engines take
addresses from the length of their paths: with OUTDIR names of different
length openboot.bin comes out the same.


8. Guests booted by hand (not part of test-all)
-----------------------------------------------
Firmware 848c07f (legion) and 8d9e574 (pci); QEMU with the vpci stack, which
starts with the TTE page-size patch (256M pages; md/legion/README, "The
guest"). Stock QEMU 8.2.2 runs legion on S10 but stalls loading the b134 kernel
(the known 256M page-size bug); pci needs the patched QEMU anyway (vpci,
cmd646, mptsas).

    config  guest                       boot device    result
    ------  --------------------------  -------------  ------------------
    legion  OpenSolaris b134 (AI ISO)   cdrom          maintenance prompt
    pci     OpenSolaris b134 (AI ISO)   cdrom, cmd646  maintenance prompt
    pci     Solaris 10 u11 (installed)  disk, cmd646   console login:
The maintenance prompt is "Enter user name for system maintenance": the live
image's behaviour when its login service does not start; both configurations
stop in the same place. Not tried: Solaris 11 (S11.1 on pci stops after `e1000g0
link up`).
